    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>Br</mi></math> is mixed with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>5</mn></msub><mi>Br</mi></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>. The resulting solution is divided into two equal parts <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mfenced></math> and treated with excess <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;solution and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;solution respectively as shown below:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> Solution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>AgNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;solution (excess) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> Solution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>BaCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;solution (excess) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math><br />The number of moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math> respectively are"
